 "notes": "Florida redrew 2026 districts mid-decade; numbers above are the 2026 districts. One source covering all 28 seats is a law-firm/lobbying client alert (Brownstein Hyatt Farber Schreck PDF), used alone for districts 1,2,3,5,6,8,10,11,12,15,17,18,19; it wrongly labels Austin Rogers (FL-2) 'incumbent' (Neal Dunn retired), so treat it as secondary and confirm against state certification (Florida Elections Canvassing Commission certifies 17 Nov 2026). The FL-11 and FL-19 background lines come from search-result summaries of campaign coverage. Close races: FL-7 Elijah +0.50% and FL-9 Soto +0.52%, both just outside the 0.5% recount threshold, AP called 10 Nov per Spectrum News 13; FL-26 Diaz-Balart +1,702 votes, AP called 9 Nov, Democrat Nicole Locklin had not conceded and disputed a vote-total correction; FL-27 Salazar +1,116, WLRN says AP called 10 Nov but also says the race triggered a mandatory recount, so it may not be final; FL-13 Luna ~49-48, AP called about 5 Nov; FL-4 Bean 50-48.3 per WGCU election-night reporting, no AP call found. Sitting members in a different district: Wasserman Schultz (was FL-25, now 20), Frankel (was 22, now 23), Moskowitz (was 23, now 25). Former FL-20 member (not in roster) did not hold FL-20; not researched why. Sitting members not returning: Dunn (retired), Mills (lost primary), Webster (retired), Buchanan (retired), Donalds (ran for governor), Wilson (retired)."
}
